config HAL_ECDSA_GEN_SIG_CM
    bool "Enable countermeasure for ECDSA signature generation"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32H2
    default n
    help
        Enable this option to apply the countermeasure for ECDSA signature operation
        This countermeasure masks the real ECDSA sign operation
        under dummy sign operations to add randomness in the generated power signature.
        This countermeasure is only necessary for ESP32-H2 < v1.2.

config HAL_ECDSA_ALLOW_ESP32P4_PRE_ECO5
    bool "Allow ECDSA peripheral on ESP32-P4 revisions before v3.0 (insecure)"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4 && ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3
    default n
    help
        By default the ESP32-P4 hardware ECDSA peripheral is disabled on chip revisions
        before v3.0 (eco5), because those revisions are vulnerable to a side-channel
        attack that can extract the private key.

        Enable this option to use the hardware ECDSA peripheral on these revisions anyway.
        Only do so if the application does not need ECDSA keys to resist physical or
        side-channel attacks.

        Note that the SECP384R1 curve is not supported by the ECDSA peripheral on these
        revisions. SECP384R1 signature verification falls back to software, and hardware
        signing with SECP384R1 keys is rejected.
